    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d30">

                <pb facs="0069" n="59" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg59"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Walter S. Robertson to General Marshall </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-08-21">21 August 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. On 19 August the Three Commissioners agreed to direct Sub-Team 25 to proceed
                    immediately to the Hsiang Ho area via Anping to investigate alleged conflicts in
                    that area. NG and CCP<anchor n="76" xml:id="d30-f1"/> Commissioners offered safe
                    conduct for the team.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d30-f1" n="76" xml:id="d30-f1-content">
                <p>National Government and Chinese Communist Party, respectively.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
